1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,540
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:28,020
Lord Death has made his decision.

3
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:32,120
This afternoon, you'll begin class on a trial basis.

4
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:35,340
I'll come to get you later on, so be sure you're ready.

5
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:38,540
You hear me?

6
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:42,740
Still nothing.

7
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:46,660
Look, I'm a zombie and I still teach classes here.

8
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:49,980
So surely someone who's still alive can make a good student.

9
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:53,460
Hello in there.

10
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:53,520
Hello.

11
00:00:53,520 --> 00:01:01,680
This kid totally hates me.

12
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:22,960
繋いだ魂の火が胸を刺すなら

13
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:29,560
言葉よりもっと強い響きが今聞こえるか

14
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:47,140
6人目も合わさず運命まで絡んでく

15
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:52,860
行き先もらったポテル 食えない夜を恥で

16
00:01:52,860 --> 00:02:02,220
不可愛しすぎた眩しさが 悪い夢に続いても

17
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:09,520
繋いだ魂の火が胸を刺すなら

18
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:16,280
言葉よりもっと強い響きが今聞こえるか

19
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:21,200
出会った訳は途絶びに 惹きつけられて

20
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:27,280
触れた瞬間の傷の分だけ確かになれる

21
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:38,440
I was talking to him for a long time trying to persuade him to come out but he was too afraid

22
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:43,480
in the end he told me that because I was a zombie he didn't know how to deal with me

23
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:49,400
okay I see he's incredibly depressed and I can't think what else to do

24
00:02:49,400 --> 00:03:04,480
his room's down that way so I finally get to see Krona you seem to have found some way to connect to and understand his soul wavelength I'd like you to teach him some things so he can become more accustomed to the academy it's no problem I'm happy to help out thank you

25
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:19,480
no she finally showed up take her around the school too while you're at it

26
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:26,480
I'm just walking in circles where am I supposed to go

27
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:34,480
Sid it's you pardon me a second I was so lost I thought I was gonna die here

28
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:38,480
you used to go to this school too Marie

29
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:45,480
the exciting and embarrassing trial enrollment the DWMA new lifestyle support fair is open

30
00:03:45,480 --> 00:04:05,480
Krona the demon swordsman a legacy of madness left by the witch Medusa who created a new form of weapon and meister when she melted down the demon sword Ragnarok mixed him into black blood and used that blood to replace Krona's own

31
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:20,480
a witch's soul is needed to turn a magic weapon into a death site in the end perhaps it is the witch who is responsible for the evolution of the weapon and not the weapons Meister

32
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:31,480
you can't stand it can you stop why hold it in that's not healthy you want to dismember everything you can't hide it from me

33
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:38,480
you're curious about him you want to study the child I created

34
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:54,480
you've been infected by the Kishin's madness I can't wait to see what happens

35
00:04:54,480 --> 00:05:09,480
coming in hey there's no one here

36
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,480
Maka

37
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:17,480
what are you doing over there I feel safer when I'm tucked in the corner like this

38
00:05:17,480 --> 00:05:24,480
come on you look like somebody's given you a time-out here stand up yeah okay

39
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,480
I'm going to show you around the Academy today

40
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:32,480
oh you are I don't know you know I'm really happy to have you here Krona

41
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:39,480
yeah

42
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:41,480
hey hey

43
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:43,480
and this lady is Miss Marie

44
00:05:43,480 --> 00:05:44,480
I'm new here too

45
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:47,480
well I'm new as a teacher anyway tomorrow is my first day

46
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:50,480
I know how you feel Krona we're in the same boat

47
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:53,480
but don't worry I'm sure we'll both do just fine

48
00:05:53,480 --> 00:06:02,480
oh okay oh I see now show him he's not alone a nice technique Marie

49
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:05,480
Kona the blue man is back again he scares me

50
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:07,480
Sid we need you to stay out here

51
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:11,480
you can relax I know Sid there looks like a big scary blue gorilla

52
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:14,480
but I promise he's actually a pretty nice guy

53
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:19,480
hey all right then we don't want to keep your education waiting anymore now do we

54
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:26,480
let's get going I wouldn't be getting too cocky now if I were you stupid humans

55
00:06:29,480 --> 00:06:31,480
hi there mini Ragnarok

56
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:33,480
oh what is that it's so cute

57
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,480
what'd you do to me you ugly cow

58
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:37,480
I don't know what you mean

59
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:40,480
what are you doing here I never agreed to be your friend

60
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:41,480
aww

61
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:45,480
I'm feeling so much closer to you now that you can't hurt me

62
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:54,480
you don't have much to look at under there do you cow

63
00:06:54,480 --> 00:07:00,480
I'm sorry I'm so sorry I didn't mean to I'll never do it again

64
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:04,480
no Krona it's okay I'm the one who should apologize

65
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,480
come on Krona quit hiding there's nothing to be afraid of here

66
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:11,480
come on Krona quit hiding there's nothing to be afraid of here

67
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:32,680
Come on, Crona, quit hiding.

68
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,540
There's nothing to be afraid of here.

69
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:57,320
It's so bright.

70
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,080
What?

71
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:02,660
Why are you laughing?

72
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:03,900
Did I say something funny?

73
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:07,000
Well, how do you like our humble academy so far?

74
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:09,600
Do you think you can get used to being here?

75
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:12,500
No, this place is definitely not for me.

76
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,680
You're just a little nervous.

77
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:16,140
You'll be fine, don't worry.

78
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,440
Uh-uh, I can't deal with this.

79
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:20,060
I want to go back to my corner.

80
00:08:21,180 --> 00:08:22,880
Maybe a nice hard kick would help.

81
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:23,400
Down, boy.

82
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:26,000
Oh, hey, I know.

83
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:27,460
Why not write some poetry?

84
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:28,840
How does that sound?

85
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:30,860
Poetry?

86
00:08:31,020 --> 00:08:32,240
You've got to be kidding me.

87
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:41,000
I write poems a lot when something's bothering me.

88
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:41,980
It really helps.

89
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:44,000
Oh, come on.

90
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:46,100
How much more emo can you possibly get?

91
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:49,120
You can talk to me if something's wrong, you know?

92
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:56,040
Why don't we try writing a poem together?

93
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:59,160
If you say so, I guess I can give it a try.

94
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:05,800
Are you all done?

95
00:09:06,260 --> 00:09:06,640
Yeah.

96
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:08,960
I want to see.

97
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:10,680
This is so stupid.

98
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:18,480
So, uh, how is it?

99
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:21,560
Huh?

100
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:25,640
This makes me wish I'd never been born.

101
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,740
It's so sad.

102
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,420
Hiya, guys!

103
00:09:29,740 --> 00:09:31,520
What are you lame-os doing in here?

104
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:32,980
The weather's amazing.

105
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:34,600
We shouldn't be locked up in school.

106
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:35,460
Let's get going.

107
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,440
Well, I guess it does get gloomy without Blackstar around.

108
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:43,300
But fear not, now that I'm here.

109
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:45,660
The sun has come out from behind the clouds.

110
00:09:46,020 --> 00:09:46,660
Read this.

111
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:53,400
I wish I'd never been born.

112
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:56,720
What's so horrible about a stupid poem?

113
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:03,600
I wish that I'd never been born.

114
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:07,360
I wish that I'd never been born.

115
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:13,820
I wish that I'd never come back to life.

116
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:15,000
What the hell, Sid?

117
00:10:15,020 --> 00:10:16,100
When did you get in here?

118
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,860
Uh, about Krona.

119
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:21,300
There are still some issues to work out.

120
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:24,400
But I do think you'll get accustomed to the Academy eventually.

121
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:25,540
Oh, good.

122
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:26,680
I'm glad to hear it.

123
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:29,400
But you're looking a little pale, Sid.

124
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:31,820
Do you think you're coming down with something?

125
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:32,720
No, no.

126
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:33,800
No, it's nothing.

127
00:10:34,620 --> 00:10:37,360
Anyway, Krona is headed for the Czech Republic right now.

128
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:41,000
I sent him along as part of Maka's supplementary lesson.

129
00:10:41,460 --> 00:10:41,940
Why?

130
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:43,380
What's wrong over there?

131
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:47,940
There's a village where the citizens spend their time creating figures known as golems.

132
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:53,220
Apparently, the oldest golem made there has suddenly gone berserk and begun destroying things.

133
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:56,020
Luckily, the damage so far seems to be light.

134
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:57,520
Hold on a sec.

135
00:10:57,580 --> 00:10:58,720
Are you for real, Sid?

136
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:00,860
For real about what?

137
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:04,480
When golems are created, they are programmed to be protectors.

138
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:08,480
Whether the damage is light so far or not, the implications here are serious.

139
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:13,080
For a golem to lose control and begin destroying things is unthinkable.

140
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:16,200
It may have something to do with the madness wavelengths.

141
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:18,680
Sid, contact Stein.

142
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:20,600
This could be very important.

143
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,020
I'd like to hear his opinion on the matter.

144
00:11:23,020 --> 00:11:27,500
So, this is Loof Village, huh?

145
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:29,560
They sure do have a lot of chimneys.

146
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:32,140
That's because they make so many golems here.

147
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:35,580
There's probably a kiln in every house.

148
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,860
Now let's eat us some souls.

149
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:42,640
Things have changed.

150
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,240
That isn't how we operate anymore.

151
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:47,420
We're going to do things differently now that we're students at the academy.

152
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:58,140
I wonder where the supposedly berserk golem that we need to find is hiding.

153
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:00,720
I'll ask the villagers for details.

154
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:04,880
These golem creators are enchanters.

155
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:19,280
They use those giant gloves of theirs to mix magic into the soil.

156
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:21,960
That's how they create the figures and bring them to life.

157
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:26,660
I can't say they look all that happy to see us in their village.

158
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:27,740
Sol!

159
00:12:29,740 --> 00:12:32,400
No one I talk to knows anything about the golem.

160
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:37,420
They're hiding something, that's for sure.

161
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,700
Hey, you guys.

162
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:44,340
I'm guessing you're here because you heard about our incident.

163
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:47,320
You're looking for the golem, the one that's gone berserk.

164
00:12:49,780 --> 00:12:51,060
My name's Giriko.

165
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:52,660
I'm an enchanter.

166
00:12:53,660 --> 00:12:55,920
I'll show you the way, just follow me.

167
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:23,380
I'm going to let go.

168
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:25,580
I'm going to find out.

169
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:28,720
I have to?

170
00:13:28,720 --> 00:13:43,260
What are you doing sitting here in the dark?

171
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:45,960
Hey, Stein?

172
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:49,000
Hey, do you hear me?

173
00:13:52,140 --> 00:13:52,820
Marie.

174
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:54,520
You okay?

175
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:55,940
Yeah, I'm fine.

176
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:57,120
What do you need?

177
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:59,420
I have a message from Lord Death.

178
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:02,660
Apparently, the oldest golem in Loof Village has gone crazy.

179
00:14:04,860 --> 00:14:07,220
Do you have any cups? I'll make us some tea.

180
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:09,000
Use those over there.

181
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:12,180
You put tea in a beaker?

182
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:17,120
Anyway, Lord Death wants to hear your opinion on the subject.

183
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:20,760
Is this incident going to be a problem for us?

184
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:23,800
Golems are usually constructed to protect against evil.

185
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:27,160
It isn't in their programming to become destructive like this.

186
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:32,040
I suppose modern technology could be used to create golems with different programming.

187
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:36,560
But then again, you said this happened to the oldest golem they have in the village.

188
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:39,460
You think the madness wavelengths have something to do with it?

189
00:14:39,460 --> 00:14:42,880
Even if they do, the order of events seems strange.

190
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:44,400
How do you mean?

191
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:51,020
Thankfully, as far as we know, there still haven't been any incidents related to the Kishan's revival and madness.

192
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:57,240
It's hard to believe that the first such incident would involve a soulless creature like the golem going crazy.

193
00:14:57,240 --> 00:15:01,740
I agree. If anything, it seems like people should be the first to be affected by it.

194
00:15:02,220 --> 00:15:05,980
So the first event we hear about shouldn't involve an object like the golem.

195
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:11,740
That's right. The golem shouldn't go berserk until the world is fully enveloped in the madness of the Kishan.

196
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:17,040
Of course, we still shouldn't take the situation too lightly.

197
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:18,460
Hold on a sec.

198
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,220
I'm going to the library.

199
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:23,600
Please ask Lord Death to give me some time to consider what's happened.

200
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:29,820
And after all that work to make us tea.

201
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:35,280
Hey, how much further do we have to go until we reach the golem?

202
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:37,140
We're almost there.

203
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:39,980
Yeah, right. That's what you keep telling us.

204
00:15:40,580 --> 00:15:43,500
You and your village are really starting to creep me out, dude.

205
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:46,840
Be quiet, soul. There's no need to be rude.

206
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:52,300
The villagers here make their living by creating golems and exporting them to other countries.

207
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:57,020
The golems ward off evil if you put them by your front door.

208
00:15:57,620 --> 00:15:59,940
You see, everyone is afraid of the unknown.

209
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:02,840
So what you're trying to say now is that we're evil?

210
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:06,800
Why are you getting so angry with them? He never said anything like that.

211
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:09,800
Not in so many words, maybe, but that's what they're thinking.

212
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:13,760
The truth is we want to live in peace and quiet.

213
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:16,920
We don't like it much when strangers come to our village.

214
00:16:17,980 --> 00:16:21,540
Which is why we try to adopt the calm of the golem and avoid conflict.

215
00:16:23,460 --> 00:16:25,340
In the end, everyone is the same.

216
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:27,560
We all have evil inside us.

217
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:32,440
Even someone who wears a mask of goodness can still have pitch darkness in his heart, you see.

218
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:34,620
What was that?

219
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:42,520
Oh, come on. If I tell you, that'll spoil all the fun.

220
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:59,020
Oh, well. I suppose there's no hiding the truth anymore.

221
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:00,460
Heads up, soul.

222
00:17:00,840 --> 00:17:02,280
Yeah, I'm already on it.

223
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:11,900
Impossible. That's crazy.

224
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:13,080
What's up, Maka?

225
00:17:13,620 --> 00:17:14,680
What's going on?

226
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:17,140
Golems aren't supposed to be living things, are they?

227
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:20,240
But I can sense a soul wavelength coming from that thing.

228
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:23,300
You're a young meister, I take it.

229
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:24,960
Looks like you figured it out.

230
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:31,000
I've been waiting for this moment for 800 years.

231
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:36,260
I use techniques I learned as an enchanter to swap my memories with my own children,

232
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:38,200
passing my brain through the generations.

233
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:41,000
I've lived out 30 boring lives.

234
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,740
800 years?

235
00:17:42,960 --> 00:17:44,300
What are you talking about?

236
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:47,740
The idea was to store up enough strength to take on death.

237
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:49,680
And his precious organization.

238
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:51,540
Your DWMA.

239
00:17:52,220 --> 00:17:53,820
But that's all over now.

240
00:17:54,460 --> 00:17:57,140
I think you children might want to start saying your goodbyes.

241
00:17:57,140 --> 00:18:01,360
What the hell is he?

242
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:03,620
You see, I don't need a meister.

243
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:07,060
The golem I created for myself will do just fine.

244
00:18:07,060 --> 00:18:18,800
This guy's a weapon?

245
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:20,800
And his golem has a soul.

246
00:18:21,660 --> 00:18:23,820
What else is wrong with this village?

247
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:30,620
Give up your attack and turn away right now.

248
